Man, I keep looking at that and going back and forth.  It does have a
certain elegance, but is also has a certain, you know, just saying codes.  I
think the main problem with this method is--what if the ISO changes the
codes, as recently happened with the language codes?  I'm not sure the
meanings of Lojban terms should be tied to the ISO codes, although I do
still think the ISO lists are a great place to start.

Oren, can you clarify what you meant by "top-level" before in terms of
language codes?

